.TH "ltsp-swapfile-delete" "8" "2026-09-11" "ltsp6"
.SH "NAME"
ltsp\-swapfile\-delete \(em Remove swap files of clients that are no longer around
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBltsp\-swapfile\-delete\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Housekeeping for the directory nbdswapd(8) fills. Clients with no local disk
get a swap file on the server, one per address, named \fIaddress\fB.swap\fR.
Nothing removes them when a client stops existing, so this runs from cron.
.PP
It takes no arguments. For every \fI*.swap\fR in the swap directory it decides
whether the client is still alive \(em an open connection in netstat(8), or an
answer to a single ping \(em and touches the file if so. Everything left
untouched for long enough is then deleted.
.SH "FILES"
.PP
.IP "\fI/etc/ltsp/ltsp.conf\fP" 4
Read if present. \fBLTSP_SWAP_DIR\fR overrides where the swap files live.
.IP "\fI/var/lib/ltsp/swapfiles/\fP" 4
The default swap directory.
.SH "BUGS"
.PP
\fBOn Debian this script deletes nothing, and says nothing about it.\fR The
last line calls \fB/usr/sbin/tmpwatch\fR, which is a Red Hat tool: Debian has
no \fBtmpwatch\fR package at all, the equivalent being \fBtmpreaper\fR. The
call therefore fails with \(lqnot found\(rq \(em and the script ends in
\fBexit 0\fR regardless, so cron records a success. The visible effect is a
swap directory that only ever grows, with no error anywhere to explain it.
.PP
Until that is fixed, either install a \fBtmpwatch\fR compatible with the
invocation, or replace the call with the Debian equivalent, which takes its
age in hours as well:
.PP
.nf
tmpreaper \-\-mtime 360h "$LTSP_SWAP_DIR"
.fi
.PP
The liveness test also needs netstat(8) from \fBnet\-tools\fR, which
ltsp\-server does not declare as a dependency and a minimal Debian install
does not necessarily have. Without it the netstat branch fails quietly and
only the ping decides \(em which marks a client dead as soon as it stops
answering ICMP, whether or not it is still using the swap file.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBnbdswapd\fP(8),
\fBtmpreaper\fP(8),
\fBnetstat\fP(8).
.SH "AVAILABILITY"
.PP
\fBltsp\-swapfile\-delete\fR is part of the \fBltsp\-server\fP package; the
latest version is available from \fIhttps://github.com/MAButz/ltsp6\fR.
